adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the code decrypts and parses the incoming `keys` with:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

There is no try/catch around `symmetricDecrypt(...)` or `JSON.parse(...)`. The decryption key explicitly falls back to an empty string (`|| ""`) if `CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY` is unset, and a malformed ciphertext (or wrong/missing key) can cause either `symmetricDecrypt` to throw or `JSON.parse` to throw. Either way, the handler will crash and Next.js will return a 500 response instead of a controlled 4xx/clear error. This is a concrete, diff-introduced correctness/reliability problem.
